.TH DANBY-ORBIT 1
.SH NAME
danby-orbit \- planar two-body orbital flight
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/orbit
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Temple/orbit
is an interactive live simulation of planar two-body orbital flight.
It integrates the model continuously and redraws its state as parameters or
initial conditions change.
.SH MODEL
R''=-mu R/|R|^3.
.PP
R is spacecraft position, mu is gravitational strength, and the initial tangential velocity determines orbit shape.
.SH DISPLAY
The central disc is the attracting body and the trail is the orbit in x-y space. Closed, open, and collision paths correspond to different energies.
.SH CONTROLS
Drag the main view or velocity track to set initial tangential speed. The bottom tracks set gravity and velocity.
.PP
Space pauses or resumes the simulation.  Period advances one displayed step
while paused.  The
.B r
key restores the default initial state and
.B q
or Escape exits.
.SH INTERPRETATION
The quantities are normalized unless physical units are stated explicitly.
The display is a visualization of a low-dimensional differential-equation
model, not an agent simulation or a prediction of a particular real system.
Parameter changes restart the displayed history so trajectories from different
settings are not joined.
.SH NUMERICS
The state is advanced by the general-purpose
.B Numerics
fourth-order Runge-Kutta solver.  Small negative values caused by numerical
roundoff are clamped for nonnegative population and stock models.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/orbit.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR numerics (2)

